  --- BFK-2018 fiducial ---
  local galactic a_theta = sqrt(abar g_bar) = 9.76e-11..1.25e-10 m/s^2  (g_bar bracket 1.1e-10..1.8e-10)
  (a) LONGITUDINAL SOUND SPEED  cbar = 425..544 km/s ;  V_sun = 233 km/s  ->  Mach 0.43..0.55  SUBSONIC
      V_crit_perp = 418..535 km/s -> the naive Landau/supersonic
      screen does NOT engage at the solar circle (the Sun is ~x2 below the critical speed).
  (b) DISRUPTION BUBBLE (infall sqrt(2GM/r) > cbar): r_dis = 0.0060..0.0098 AU
      vs Mercury 0.387 AU: the bubble is x39+ inside Mercury -- protects NOTHING
      planetary. (And structurally: the Sun's mass sources phonons in the INTACT region r > r_dis
      regardless -- excising a 0.01-AU core does not turn off the Sun-sourced phonon force at planets.)
  (c) COHERENCE: lambda_dB = 1.60 mm vs interparticle l = 13.6 um -> ratio 118 >> 1: coherent at planetary radii (B-K's own premise holds there)
  (d) HEALING LENGTH xi = hbar/(m cbar) = 0.12 mm -- no AU-scale decoherence scale exists
  (e) SUPERLUMINAL BREAKDOWN: around the Sun a_theta(r) = sqrt(abar GM)/r -> cbar(r) = c at
      r = 10.4 AU: INSIDE this radius the published dispersion gives cbar > c --
      the non-relativistic phonon EFT is formally out of its domain for r < 10.4 AU
      (Mercury..Saturn inside or at the edge). This is the one computed sense in which the EFT
      'breaks down near stars' -- but it removes PREDICTIVITY, not the force: the static background
      solution a_phi = sqrt(abar a_b) is what the theory offers, and perturbations about it are
      superluminal. No screening mechanism emerges from the published EFT at planetary radii.
